//! task: write
//! ask: Declare a little-endian wire header: a 16-bit magic, a byte, and a 32-bit payload length.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §5.2
//! explain: `:minor` is little-endian and `:maior` big-endian; both are contextual words. Each multi-byte field names its order, and the struct is packed with no padding, so this header is seven bytes on the wire: 2 + 1 + 4.

@transitus
publica structura Cabecera {
    magia:  u16:minor
    genus:  u8
    onus:   u32:minor
}
